  "articleBody": "Deciding whether to DIY your baseboard installation or call in a professional can be tricky. Here are some clear signs that getting expert help is probably the best route for your project: \n*   **Your walls or floors aren’t perfectly level.** When things aren’t plumb and square, fitting baseboards neatly becomes a serious challenge. Pros know how to work with imperfections to make it look seamless.\n*   **You need to match existing trim profiles.** If you’re adding on or doing a partial remodel, ensuring new baseboards blend perfectly with old ones takes a keen eye and specific tools that a professional brings.\n*   **The project involves long runs or many intricate corners.** Long stretches of baseboard or rooms with lots of ins and outs increase the difficulty significantly, making precision critical for a polished look.\n*   **You're aiming for a high-finish painted result.** If you want a smooth, flawless painted finish, any gap or inconsistency in the baseboard installation will stand out. Professionals ensure the foundation is perfect for painting.\n*   **You want consistent reveal and tight wall contact.** Achieving that clean, consistent line where the baseboard meets the wall and floor is harder than it looks and is a hallmark of professional work. \nFor homes in Aurora and the greater Denver area, HH Remodeling LLC offers the expertise to handle these challenges, ensuring your baseboard installation is done right and looks fantastic.",
